Error [jet.ValueNotSendable]: `cell` can't cross into a task because `Cell<Int>` isn't sendable
  --> tests/ui/local_cell_crossing.jet:4:18
    |
  4 |     worker: task {
    |                  ^
 Why: `Cell` owns thread-local state and must stay on the thread that created it; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: Create the `Cell<T>` inside the task, or use `Shared<T>` for synchronized state
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1102

Error [jet.ValueNotSendable]: `Cell`<Int> cannot be stored in `Shared<T>`
  --> tests/ui/local_cell_crossing.jet:11:15
    |
 11 |     _: Shared{cell}
    |               ^^^^
 Why: A Cell and its guards own one-thread borrow state; wrapping that state does not make it synchronized
 Fix: Store the value itself in `Shared<T>`, then read and write its fields directly
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1102

Error [jet.ValueNotSendable]: `LocalCache` cannot be stored in `Shared<T>`
  --> tests/ui/local_cell_crossing.jet:19:15
    |
 19 |     _: Shared{cache}
    |               ^^^^^
 Why: A Cell and its guards own one-thread borrow state; wrapping that state does not make it synchronized
 Fix: Store the value itself in `Shared<T>`, then read and write its fields directly
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1102

Error [jet.ValueNotSendable]: `cell` can't be captured by an HTTP handler because `Cell<Int>` isn't sendable
  --> tests/ui/local_cell_crossing.jet:25:18
    |
 25 |     mux.get("/", fn(req: HTTPRequest) {
    |                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: HTTP handlers are retained by the server and invoked on request workers, so their captured state must be owned and thread-safe
 Fix: Capture only owned sendable values in the HTTP handler, or use `Shared<T>` for synchronized state
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1102
